<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">gryphon-rider</ansi>

The Gryphon Rider is a skirmisher. It dives from the sky past the enemy's
front line onto the rows behind it, and its default aim is the healers and
casters that stand there. Between dives it fights on as an ordinary spear or
sword fighter in medium armor with a buckler. It has no creed: no alignment
gate stands in front of any of its routes.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What the Gryphon Rider is</ansi>

  Health      5 to start, 0.8 a level to level 20 (<ansi fg="command">help health</ansi>)
  Skill       Attack 1.0 and Evasion 1.0 a level, like a warrior (<ansi fg="command">help evasion</ansi>)
  Gear        medium armor, a buckler or no shield, spears and swords
              (<ansi fg="command">help armor</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help shields</ansi>)
  Stats       speed 4, strength 3, perception 2, vitality 1 (<ansi fg="command">help growth</ansi>)
  Starter kit an iron short spear, a leather buckler, a padded jack, a leather
              cap, worn boots, food, a waterskin and a knapsack
  Utility     Keen Eye (<ansi fg="command">help specialists</ansi>)

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks of the Gryphon Rider</ansi>

  Level 1   <ansi fg="yellow">Dive</ansi>        the rider's whole turn, once every 3 combat rounds: a stooping
            blow that may pass a standing front-row foe to strike the middle
            or back row, as long as the foe stands in the rider's column or
            the next. A foe's guardian can still step in for it. The rider
            has -10 Evasion until its next turn.
  Level 3   <ansi fg="yellow">Talons</ansi>      a Dive that lands leaves the foe bleeding (<ansi fg="command">help statuses</ansi>).
  Level 8   <ansi fg="yellow">Power dive</ansi>  a Dive deals 25% more damage.

Level 5 brings the first talent: Keen Edge, Footwork, Toughness, Sharp Eye
(+3% critical chance on every blow) or Wing Drill (Dive ready a round
sooner; once) (<ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>). At level 10 a Gryphon Rider promotes to a
Gryphon Knight, Skyscout or Wyvern Rider (<ansi fg="command">help gryphon-rider-routes</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Where it can fly</ansi>

The gryphon needs open sky. Indoors, in caves and on narrow ground (the
battle says when the ground folds both lines into two columns) it cannot
fly: there is no Dive, and the rider fights as an ordinary spear fighter.
A Dive also needs a melee weapon in hand.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How a Gryphon Rider fights</ansi>

A battle plays out on its own, so everything above happens without a command.
The rider's default target rule is <ansi fg="command">healers</ansi>: healers first, then casters, then
the weakest foe (<ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>). It can aim at any foe within a column of
its own because of the Dive; on the rounds the Dive is not ready, a blow at a
foe behind a standing front-liner is caught by the front-liner, as any blow
is (<ansi fg="command">help formation</ansi>). A Dive is the rider's turn: it does not also swing. Put
it in the front or middle row, with a guardian beside it (<ansi fg="command">help guardian</ansi>)
to cover the Evasion it spends. <ansi fg="command">strategy me abilities off</ansi> keeps the rider
on the ground.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Other Gryphon Riders</ansi>

A Gryphon Rider companion fights the same way, by its strategy, and promotes
and chooses talents like any other (<ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>). Recruits are hired like
any other and arrive with an iron short spear and a buckler. The gryphon
itself is not a mount you stable or feed; it is the rider's own.

Commands: <ansi fg="command">archetype</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">class</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">talent</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">strategy</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help gryphon-rider-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help abilities</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help classes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help archetype</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>.
